WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:03.670
Social skills are an integral part of culture and the workforce.

1
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:04.530
At work,

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.730
you will have an opportunity to interact with

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.029
clients who have different cultural backgrounds and experiences.

4
00:00:10.449 --> 00:00:11.289
Consequently,

5
00:00:11.449 --> 00:00:14.810
it is important to be able to demonstrate culturally competent

6
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.450
and appropriately inclusive behavior when interacting with people

7
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.149
from cultures and backgrounds different from your own.

8
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.280
Of course,

9
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.350
knowing all the nuances for every culture is impossible,

10
00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:29.100
which is why social skills are important for emotional intelligence.

11
00:00:29.799 --> 00:00:31.379
Willingness to understand,

12
00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:32.319
appreciate,

13
00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:34.580
and experience cultural diversity

14
00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:37.419
will help you develop greater communication skills

15
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.119
and cultural competency.

16
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.509
Awareness of your own biases,

17
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.319
power,

18
00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.360
and preconceived ideas of various populations

19
00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:48.740
is essential to be an effective culturally competent worker.

20
00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:50.869
By recognizing your privileges,

21
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.979
you can begin to understand the disadvantages other cultures experience.

22
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.919
It is important to be aware that your personal views

23
00:00:57.919 --> 00:01:01.139
and beliefs may have an impact on your client's life.

24
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.439
Consequently,

25
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.699
it behooves you to practice monitoring your own reactions

26
00:01:05.839 --> 00:01:07.199
while interacting with them.

27
00:01:07.839 --> 00:01:08.550
After all,

28
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.760
you will probably express your own beliefs

29
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.750
non-verbally through such things as facial expressions,

30
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.790
speech patterns,

31
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.760
and the like.

32
00:01:16.239 --> 00:01:17.660
Mistakes are inevitable.

33
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.760
Discuss them with your supervisor or instructor so that

34
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.519
you can move forward by learning from the situation.

35
00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:26.629
Dwelling on the mistake is not going to change it,

36
00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:30.239
so it is helpful to focus on how it can be handled better next time.